    "q-167616": {
      "dom_id": "question-167616",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "$\\int \\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$+\\,C$",
      "worked_solution": "We take the constant factor out of the integral and then apply the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int {x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\cdot (\\frac{{x}^{(-2+1)}}{-2+1})+C \\\\  & =4\\cdot (\\frac{{x}^{-1}}{-1})+C \\\\  & =-4\\cdot {x}^{-1}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
