    "q-167617": {
      "dom_id": "question-167617",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given that $A=2$ and $B=4,$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\int \\frac{f(x)}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$+\\,C.$",
      "worked_solution": "We found that $A=2$ and $B=4$ in steps 2 and 3, respectively. Hence, $f(x)=2{x}^{2}-4.$  \n\nUsing the sum and constant factor rules and our result from step 4, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{f(x)}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2{x}^{2}-4}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x+\\frac{4}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "",
          "tag": "mathquill",
          "choices": [],
