    "q-167618": {
      "dom_id": "question-167618",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "If $k(x)=g(x)-f(x),$ where $A=2$ and $B=4,$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}k}{\\text{d}x}=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .",
      "worked_solution": "We found that $A=2$ and $B=4$ in steps 3 and 4, respectively. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =g(x)-f(x) \\\\  & =2{e}^{x}-(2{x}^{2}-4) \\\\  & =2{e}^{x}-2{x}^{2}+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the addition and power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}k}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{e}^{x}-2{x}^{2}+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{e}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\  & =2{e}^{x}-4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
